.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt OPENSSL-FIPS 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openssl-fips
.Nd optional strict OpenSSL provider profile
.Sh DESCRIPTION
5BSD builds and packages a self-contained OpenSSL FIPS provider by default.
It is not loaded by the normal OpenSSL configuration.
The 5BSD integration build is not a FIPS-validated cryptographic module;
it identifies itself as not validated.
Formal compliance requires a validated module and adherence to its certificate,
security policy, operating environment, and entropy requirements.
.Pp
To provision the optional profile, run on the target system after the final
module has been installed, stripped, and (if applicable) code-signed:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
umask 022
OPENSSL_CONF=/dev/null openssl fipsinstall \
    -pedantic -self_test_onload \
    -module /usr/lib/ossl-modules/fips.so \
    -out /etc/ssl/fipsmodule.cnf.new
.Ed
Only after that command succeeds, publish the configuration:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mv /etc/ssl/fipsmodule.cnf.new /etc/ssl/fipsmodule.cnf
.Ed
The destination directory must be writable only by the administrator.
Provision each target separately; do not copy installation success records
from a build host or execute target binaries during a cross build.
The configuration uses on-load self-tests.
Repeat provisioning after every change to the module, including code signing.
An update of an already strict installation must provision and test the new
module and configuration together in its inactive boot environment.
.Pp
Select the profile for an application using:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
OPENSSL_CONF=/etc/ssl/openssl-fips.cnf application
.Ed
The profile loads the FIPS and base providers and requires
.Li fips=yes
for default algorithm fetches.
It does not enable the default or legacy providers.
Unavailable algorithms fail instead of falling back.
Applications can override OpenSSL configuration and property queries;
this profile is not system-wide enforcement and does not cover other crypto
libraries or low-level APIs.
Test applications before selecting it, especially TLS peers and old keys.
.Pp
The module is kept as its original standalone ELF file.
Its integrity MAC covers the exact module bytes and is independent of 5BSD
code-signing trust; it is not a publisher authentication signature.
Do not strip, repack, or append a signature after generating its configuration.
.Sh BUILD OPTIONS
.Va WITHOUT_OPENSSL_FIPS
omits the provider and profile.
It does not change the ordinary default provider.
The portable provider currently uses C implementations; normal OpenSSL's
assembly implementations are unchanged.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/lib/ossl-modules/fips.so
.It Pa /usr/lib/ossl-modules/fips.so
Optional provider, shipped in the OpenSSL package.
.It Pa /etc/ssl/openssl-fips.cnf
Opt-in strict profile.
.It Pa /etc/ssl/fipsmodule.cnf
Locally provisioned module integrity configuration.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openssl-fipsinstall 1 ,
.Xr config 5 ,
.Xr fips_config 5 ,
.Xr fips_module 7
